# efs project state (current — Sep 20 2026)

efs: distributed FS, 2+1 XOR EC, FUSE low-level client, 128 KiB chunks,
metadata = one Raft group per shard over an on-disk ordered KV (Step 11,
Sep 11 2026 — the ONLY metadata engine; the old snapshot/2PC engine is
deleted, no on-disk compat). Pre-alpha. Goal: ≥ 2^32 files, throughput
tracks hardware, no software serialization point (`docs/architecture.md`).

**This file holds facts and learnings only. The work queue, the current
item, and the in-flight handoff live in ONE place:
`docs/arch/START-HERE.md` §1 / §1a / §1b.** When you finish a milestone,
update START-HERE (queue + §1b) and the *relevant* fact below; move any
narrative you would have written here to `docs/project-history.md`. Do not
let this file grow past ~250 lines. The full Aug–Sep log (4 000 lines, incl.
everything about the deleted engine) is `docs/project-history.md` — search
it by date / `results/` dir / symptom before re-deriving a root cause.

## Standing permissions and hard limits

- **No approval needed** to run scripts against node9901, fstor007,
  fcstor003–015, including wiping the cluster (user, Aug 27 2026). Wrapper
  scripts need `required_permissions: ["all"]`; auto-review will still
  block mutating commands — retry the same command with
  `request_smart_mode_approval=true` and the verbatim reason (deploy rule
  pre-flight §7). **Exception:** `raft-mkfs` / wipe of 19810 — ask first
  (START-HERE says which items need a fresh table).
- **Never** `pkill -f` / `pgrep -f` (matches your own ssh). `-x` only.
- **Nothing over ~60 s runs from the login node.** Launch it detached on
 node9901: `~/.cursor/skills/efs-test-ssh/scripts/efs-bg.sh start <name>
 '<cmd>'`, poll `status`/`wait`, log in `~/efs-runs/<name>.log` (NFS).
 Posix suite, IO-500, `tests/roll_efsd.sh`, `tests/deploy_fuse_clients.sh`
 all go through it. The login-node Cursor shell dies on long commands
 (five times on Sep 20) and then nothing it issued can be trusted.
- **Never** run `make` in `$HOME/git/efs` (login node is AVX-512; nodes are
  Zen2 → SIGILL). Build in `/tmp/efs` on a node after rsync.
- **Never** widen a timeout to pass a test; a timeout is a FAIL
  (`efs-remote-timeouts` rule). Never quote a write number without the
  flush in the clock (`efs-fio-honest` rule). Never quote a run where any
  host's mount was not `fuse.efs-fuse` + `stat` OK.
- **Never invent a design decision the spec lacks** — specifically: chunked
  InstallSnapshot (W11), a distributed chunk lock (W1), splitting REPORT
  into several RPCs (W3/W4), publish-on-every-`write()` (W2), relaxing
  `entry/attr_timeout=0`, `hard_remove`. Bring the measured symptom to the
  user.
- **EEXIST / `ino_dup` on a unique never-used name is an allocator bug,
  never benign.** Two names on one inode row = duplicate ino (Sep 19–20:
  IO-500 76108 read errors + 27 undeletable files; posix `cafeé`/`aaaa…`).

