  just-edited file — `rsync --checksum` if a node builds stale.
- Kernel: `ptrace_scope=0`, `perf_event_paranoid=1`, `kptr_restrict=0` on
  all 15 hosts, **runtime only** (`sysctl -w`, reverts on reboot; ask the
  user to re-apply, never edit `/etc/sysctl.d`). `strace -p`, `gdb -p`,
  `perf record -a/-g` with kernel symbols all work same-uid. Attach to a
  RUNNING daemon; never start a daemon under strace.
- Leftover inert dangling dentries on 19810 (from the dup-ino bug, before
  the   fix): `/io500/easyv` (26), `/io500/2026.09.19-22.52.15/ior-easy`
  (27), `/posix-fcstor007-93jwgp99/names_unicode_nfc_nfd_coexist/cafeé`
  (parent ino 650, the `alloc_key_claim` repro). `rm` → ENOENT, `rmdir` →
  ENOTEMPTY, by design; ignore or wipe.
- A dead `efs-fuse` leaves `/tmp/efs-mount` as a plain dir or a
  "Transport endpoint is not connected" corpse — everything reads ENOENT /
  fio shows `Disk stats: md0`. That is NOT data loss: `findmnt` + `stat`
  before believing a disappearance (deploy rule pre-flight §5).

